#!/bin/bash
# Builds the Engine image for browser pipelines as linux/amd64 and pushes it to a registry, tagged with
# the commit it was built from (docs/stable/homelab-arr/work-items/WI-1100-publishable-image.md).
#
#   RUNLINE_REGISTRY=forgejo.example/owner deploy/publish-image             # build and push
#   RUNLINE_REGISTRY=forgejo.example/owner deploy/publish-image --no-push   # build only, in the local daemon
#
# Configuration comes from the environment, never from this file:
#   RUNLINE_REGISTRY   registry host and path the image goes under, no tag and no credentials
#                      (forgejo.example/owner gives forgejo.example/owner/runline-engine-browser:<tag>)
#   RUNLINE_EXTRA_TAG  optional; a second tag for the same image, such as the release tag v1.2.0 that a
#                      release workflow builds from (docs/stable/homelab-arr/work-items/WI-1101-forgejo-action.md).
#                      It is added beside the commit tag, never in its place; `latest` is refused
#
# Registry credentials are not read or stored here. Log in beforehand with `docker login "$host"`; the
# password is then read from the terminal or a credential helper (`--password-stdin` from a secret
# manager), never given on a command line. The push uses that login.
#
# The tag is the first 12 characters of the commit id: nothing floats, so a deployment names exactly
# what it runs and can be rolled back to a tag. A tree with uncommitted or untracked changes is not
# pushed (what runs could not be found from the tag); with --no-push it builds, tagged `<commit>-dirty`.
#
# The image is linux/amd64 only (Google ships Chrome for nothing else). On an arm64 machine the Docker
# daemon must be able to run amd64 containers (Rosetta; Colima: vmType vz, rosetta true) and the entry
# says so when it cannot.
set -euo pipefail

fail() { printf 'publish-image: %s\n' "$*" >&2; exit 1; }

push=yes
case "${1:-}" in
  "") ;;
  --no-push) push=no ;;
  *) fail "unknown argument '$1' (the only one is --no-push)" ;;
esac

# The registry is checked first: nothing is built for a push that cannot happen.
registry="${RUNLINE_REGISTRY:-}"
[ -n "$registry" ] || fail "RUNLINE_REGISTRY is not set: give the registry host and path, e.g. RUNLINE_REGISTRY=forgejo.example/owner"
case "$registry" in
  *@*|*://*|*:latest|*[[:space:]]*) fail "RUNLINE_REGISTRY must be a host and path only (no credentials, scheme or tag): '${registry//@*/@...}'" ;;
esac
registry="${registry%/}"

# The extra tag is checked with the registry: nothing is built for a tag that cannot be pushed.
extra_tag="${RUNLINE_EXTRA_TAG:-}"
if [ -n "$extra_tag" ]; then
  [ "$extra_tag" != latest ] || fail "RUNLINE_EXTRA_TAG must not be 'latest': nothing floats"
  printf '%s' "$extra_tag" | grep -Eq '^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,127}$' \
    || fail "RUNLINE_EXTRA_TAG '$extra_tag' is not a valid image tag (letters, digits, '_', '.', '-'; up to 128; not starting with '.' or '-')"
fi

root="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"
cd "$root"

commit="$(git rev-parse --short=12 HEAD)" || fail "this is not a git checkout; the tag comes from the commit"
tag="$commit"
if [ -n "$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all)" ]; then
  if [ "$push" = yes ]; then
    fail "the working tree has uncommitted or untracked changes, so the image could not be found again from its tag $commit; commit them (or stash) and run again. (--no-push builds it locally anyway)"
  fi
  tag="$commit-dirty"
fi
image="$registry/runline-engine-browser:$tag"

command -v docker >/dev/null || fail "docker is not installed"
docker info >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail "the Docker daemon cannot be reached (is Docker, or Colima, running?)"

# An amd64 container must run here. Only a run proves it; the architecture of the host does not.
base="$(sed -n 's/^FROM \(eclipse-temurin[^ ]*\) AS engine$/\1/p' deploy/docker/Dockerfile)"
[ -n "$base" ] || fail "cannot find the base image in deploy/docker/Dockerfile"
# The base image is fetched first, apart from the probe: when it is not local Docker prints its download
# progress, and that must not end up in the architecture value that is compared.
docker pull --quiet --platform linux/amd64 "$base" >/dev/null || fail "cannot fetch the base image $base for linux/amd64 (is the registry reachable?)"
arch="$(docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64 --entrypoint uname "$base" -m 2>&1)" || arch=""
if [ "$arch" != "x86_64" ]; then
  fail "this Docker daemon cannot run linux/amd64 containers (got '${arch:-nothing}'). On an arm64 machine enable amd64 emulation: Colima with vmType vz and rosetta true (colima start --vm-type vz --vz-rosetta), Docker Desktop with Rosetta. QEMU is not enough: Chrome aborts under it."
fi

./gradlew --console=plain :engine:engineDistribution

docker build --platform linux/amd64 --target browser --build-context deploy=deploy \
  --label "org.opencontainers.image.revision=$(git rev-parse HEAD)" \
  -f deploy/docker/Dockerfile -t "$image" engine/build/engine-dist

built="$(docker image inspect --format '{{.Os}}/{{.Architecture}}' "$image")"
[ "$built" = "linux/amd64" ] || fail "the image came out as $built, not linux/amd64; it is not pushed"

images=("$image")
if [ -n "$extra_tag" ]; then
  extra_image="$registry/runline-engine-browser:$extra_tag"
  docker tag "$image" "$extra_image"
  images+=("$extra_image")
fi

# The commit tag goes first: the extra tag appears in the registry only after the image it names is there.
if [ "$push" = yes ]; then
  for pushed in "${images[@]}"; do docker push "$pushed"; done
fi
printf '%s\n' "${images[@]}"
